From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yanghan Ye <yyh94306@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 09:20:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha restart PHY state machine after paired replay

The paired USXGMII replay reinitializes the PHY while phylink remains
running.  A successful PHY reset can leave phylib in NOLINK with the
carrier already invalidated; the normal state-machine transition back to
PHY_UP is then skipped, leaving the carrier down until an interface
down/up.  Restart the PHY state machine after replay has been balanced,
using the same public stop/start contract as a normal interface restart.

This runs under RTNL and outside the PHY mutex.  It does not close the
netdev or re-enter phylink while replay is disabled.

Assisted-by: Codex:GPT-6-Astra
Signed-off-by: Yanghan Ye <yyh94306@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
index 9e586c6..9f1f3c0 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
@@ -4336,5 +4336,10 @@ static void airoha_usxgmii_recovery_work(struct work_struct *work)
 	/* Synchronize PHY state before balancing replay on PHY errors or recovery. */
 	phylink_replay_link_end(dev->phylink);
+	if (!ret) {
+		/* Restart polling as a normal PHY stop/start cycle would. */
+		phy_stop(phy);
+		phy_start(phy);
+	}
 	WRITE_ONCE(dev->usxgmii_recovery_running, false);
 	if (ret)
 		netdev_err(netdev, "USXGMII paired PHY replay failed: %d\n", ret);
